WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.449
what you're trying to do in training is
you're trying to get people to think

00:00:03.449 --> 00:00:07.230
trying to get people to think on their
own and that is the most beautiful thing

00:00:07.230 --> 00:00:11.130
that you want as a leaders you want all
your people thinking and you want them

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:14.700
to be able to think with a completely
open minded mind that's been completely

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:19.230
freed from constraints and the way that
you do that one of the ways that you do

00:00:19.230 --> 00:00:22.890
that one of the methodologies you can
use to do that is everybody's got their

00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:30.210
box right that they're stuck in so you
formulate a problem that the only way

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:34.020
that they're going to solve the problem
is to get outside of that box and you

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:37.380
know one of the one of the best ones is
you put somebody in a situation where

00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:40.739
you put parameters on them and you say
hey no matter what you're not allowed to

00:00:40.739 --> 00:00:44.969
go across this line hmm and then you put
in a situation would have to cross that

00:00:44.969 --> 00:00:49.170
line and the only way they're gonna win
us across that line and then they come

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:51.960
back and they said well you did told me
not to cross that line you know what I

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:55.079
didn't tell you get you all your guys
killed or I didn't tell you to to not

00:00:55.079 --> 00:00:59.489
make that investment even in this
critical situation or I didn't tell you

00:00:59.489 --> 00:01:04.920
not to do that if we had an ecological
disaster that was going on right so you

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:10.740
need to train people to use common sense
mm-hmm that's what you want to train me

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:16.650
to do and it's very hard you'd be
surprised at how at how constrained

00:01:16.650 --> 00:01:23.009
people's brains get mine yours everybody
we get stuck and so it's great to do

00:01:23.009 --> 00:01:26.939
drilling and training where you are
actually opening up the mind and freeing

00:01:26.939 --> 00:01:31.710
the mind from any kind of constraint
where you can see things from varied

00:01:31.710 --> 00:01:36.259
perspectives that are different from
your own and you can see outlets and

00:01:36.259 --> 00:01:41.970
solutions that you would never have seen
if you trap yourself inside your box and

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:46.110
those are the kind of training scenarios
that are outstanding and those the kind

00:01:46.110 --> 00:01:51.180
of training scenarios that make people
better leaders and better decision

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:55.020
makers because the key thing that they
learn how to do is they learn how to

00:01:55.020 --> 00:02:00.360
detach even at that moment we talk about
it all the time but if you can't detach

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:04.320
from that situation you can't detach far
enough away from the picture to see that

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:07.229
the only way you're going to solve this
problem is by going across that line

00:02:07.229 --> 00:02:12.690
that you were told not to go across if
you can't make that detachment you're

00:02:12.690 --> 00:02:14.730
never
across that line you're never going to

00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:18.720
open your mind you're never going to see
that solution and that is a horrible

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:21.770
trap to be stuck in

